    "narrative": "As we navigate the final stretch of the 2026 campaign, our focus for Ghost Ride the WHIP remains squarely on volume and speed efficiency. **Travis Bazzana** headlines our lineup today with a 60.94 score, anchored by a favorable matchup against Nick Martinez. While we are awaiting official confirmation, his expected slotting in the two-hole against a 4.63 xERA arm provides the exact type of high-leverage opportunity we prioritize. With the rest of our primary speed threats, including **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, **Brice Turang**, and **Edwin Arroyo**, sidelined by team off-days, our offensive ceiling is lower than usual. Consequently, we are leaning into our high-OBP stalwarts like **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Seiya Suzuki** to stabilize our AVG while hoping **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Josh Naylor** can capitalize on any late-inning mistakes to buoy our HR and RBI totals.\n\nThe decision to limit our exposure today is driven by the lack of elite-tier matchups across the board, which effectively turns this into a preservation play for our game caps. **Max Muncy** and **Isaac Paredes** were the most difficult exclusions from the starting nine; while both offer solid power floors, their sub-40 scores against middle-of-the-road pitching prompted us to bench them in favor of maintaining our daily cap discipline. **James Wood**, **Trevor Story**, and **Mickey Moniak** remain on the periphery, held out due to unfavorable park factors that suppress their projected scoring below our 40-point threshold. We are also monitoring the development of **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, **Cole Young**, and **Moises Ballesteros**, who remain in reserve as we evaluate their late-season platoon splits. Aside from the lineup uncertainty surrounding **Travis Bazzana**, the primary risk today is the lack of stolen base upside given the roster\u2019s current composition; we are effectively playing a \"hold\" strategy, banking on **Gabriel Moreno** and **Tyler Soderstrom** to provide steady production behind the plate while we wait for a more favorable schedule turn for our elite speedsters.",
